P("tedious","From Latin taediosus, from taedium “weariness, disgust.”",[C("tedious.s1","work","Filling out the same form by hand for three hours was tedious.","連續三小時手動填寫同一份表格，令人覺得冗長乏味。","tedious + task or activity","Adjective: too long, slow, or dull to hold interest.","The repeated work is dull and prolonged, which matches the first sense."),C("tedious.s2","daily life","The tedious delays at every checkpoint annoyed the travelers.","每個檢查站都令人厭煩的延誤惹惱了旅客。","tedious + repeated annoyance","Adjective: annoying because the same thing continues without change.","The repeated delays illustrate the annoying, unchanging quality of the second sense.")],[M("The tedious lecture was so lively and brief that nobody lost interest.","The tedious lecture was so long and dull that several students lost interest.","Tedious describes something too long, slow, or dull to hold interest.","meaning")],[Q("tedious.q1","tedious.s1","meaning","Why might copying thousands of identical records feel tedious?","The task is long and dull.","The records are impossible to read because they are underwater.","The task takes only a second and is exciting.","The first sense is too long, slow, or dull to hold interest."),Q("tedious.q2","tedious.s2","context","Which situation best fits tedious?","A machine repeats the same irritating delay all afternoon.","A one-time surprise party delights the guests.","A short race ends in seconds.","The repeated unchanging delay fits the annoying sense."),Q("tedious.q3","tedious.s1","distinction","What is the main effect of a tedious presentation?","Its length or dullness makes it hard to stay interested.","It is necessarily dangerous to attend.","It contains no spoken words at all.","Tedious concerns length, slowness, or dullness that loses interest."),Q("tedious.q4","tedious.s2","word-choice","Choose the natural phrase.","tedious repeated checks","tedious delicious cake","tedious suddenly arrived guest","Repeated checks can be tedious because they continue without change.")]);
P("tedium","From Latin taedium “weariness, disgust,” related to taedere “to weary.”",[C("tedium.s1","office","The tedium of sorting identical receipts made the afternoon seem endless.","整理一模一樣收據的沉悶讓整個下午彷彿沒有盡頭。","the tedium of + activity","Noun: boredom caused by something dull, repetitive, or drawn out.","The repeated sorting is the cause of boredom, matching the source sense.")],[M("The tedium of the routine kept everyone fascinated and eager for more.","The tedium of the routine bored everyone with its repetition.","Tedium is boredom caused by dull or repetitive activity.","meaning")],[Q("tedium.q1","tedium.s1","meaning","What does tedium describe?","Boredom caused by a dull or repetitive experience.","A device that sends messages by electrical signals.","A person aged from thirteen to nineteen.","Tedium is boredom caused by something dull, repetitive, or drawn out."),Q("tedium.q2","tedium.s1","context","Why did the clerk complain about the tedium of data entry?","Entering the same details repeatedly was boring.","The computer sent a message to a distant receiver.","The clerk was measuring remote weather conditions.","Repetition and dullness cause the boredom called tedium."),Q("tedium.q3","tedium.s1","distinction","Which is a likely cause of tedium?","An identical task that takes all day.","A brief, varied game with constant surprises.","A clear measurement sent from a satellite.","A drawn-out repetitive task is a typical cause of tedium."),Q("tedium.q4","tedium.s1","collocation","Which phrase is natural?","the tedium of waiting in a slow line","the tedium of a joyful surprise that lasts a second","the tedium telegraphed to the receiver","Tedium commonly names boredom caused by a prolonged activity.")]);
P("teem","Possibly from Old English tēman “to produce, bring forth”; the history of the modern sense “be full of” is uncertain.",[C("teem.s1","nature","The tide pools teem with small crabs after the water recedes.","退潮後，潮池裡滿是小螃蟹。","teem with + many people or things","Verb: to be full of a lot of people, animals, or things.","The pool contains crabs in great numbers, the first sense."),C("teem.s2","weather","Rain teemed down on the roof throughout the night.","整夜大雨傾盆落在屋頂上。","rain teems down","Verb: (of rain) to fall very heavily.","This uses the separate weather sense, with rain falling heavily.")],[M("The beach teemed with visitors, but only one person could be seen there.","The beach teemed with visitors, with people crowding the shore.","Teem with means be full of many people or things.","meaning")],[Q("teem.q1","teem.s1","meaning","If a garden teems with bees, what is true?","Many bees are present there.","Rain is falling lightly from a clear sky.","The garden has been closed for winter.","The first sense means to be full of many living things or objects."),Q("teem.q2","teem.s2","context","What does “rain teemed down” mean?","Rain fell very heavily.","The rain stopped before it began.","The rain formed a message on a wire.","The second sense is used of rain falling heavily."),Q("teem.q3","teem.s1","collocation","Which phrase uses the crowded sense?","The reef teems with colorful fish.","The reef teems down with fish.","The reef is teeming rain on fish.","Teem with describes a place being full of many things."),Q("teem.q4","teem.s2","distinction","Which sentence uses the rain sense?","Rain teemed down as the hikers reached shelter.","The station teemed with commuters.","The meadow teemed with wildflowers.","Only the first sentence describes heavy rainfall; the others use ‘full of.’")]);
