P("teenager","Formed from teen + -ager, from the numerals thirteen through nineteen.",[C("teenager.s1","school","The teenager volunteered to tutor younger students after class.","這名青少年自願在課後輔導年紀較小的學生。","a teenager aged + number","Noun: a boy or girl aged from thirteen to nineteen.","The sentence refers to someone in the defined age range."),C("teenager.s2","growing up","As a teenager, he began making more decisions for himself.","成為青少年後，他開始為自己做更多決定。","as a teenager","Noun: a young person still growing from childhood toward adult life.","The context emphasizes development toward adulthood, the second sense.")],[M("The teenager was a toddler who had not yet reached the age of thirteen.","The teenager was a sixteen-year-old who had not yet reached adulthood.","A teenager is aged thirteen to nineteen and is growing toward adulthood.","meaning")],[Q("teenager.q1","teenager.s1","meaning","What age range identifies a teenager?","Thirteen through nineteen.","Three through nine.","Thirty through ninety.","The first sense gives the specific thirteen-to-nineteen range."),Q("teenager.q2","teenager.s2","context","Why might a story focus on a teenager becoming independent?","The character is growing from childhood toward adult life.","The character is transmitting data from a satellite.","The character is measuring a property boundary.","The second sense emphasizes development from childhood toward adulthood."),Q("teenager.q3","teenager.s1","distinction","Which person is a teenager?","A seventeen-year-old apprentice.","A twelve-year-old child.","A twenty-year-old adult.","Seventeen is within the defined age range."),Q("teenager.q4","teenager.s2","word-choice","Choose the natural sentence.","The teenager learned to manage a first part-time job.","The teenager the telephone signal loudly.","The teenager was a measurement sent from space.","The noun names a young person developing toward adult life.")]);
P("teens","From teen + plural -s; teen is a shortening based on thirteen through nineteen.",[C("teens.s1","age","He moved to another city in his late teens.","他在十幾歲後期搬到另一座城市。","in one’s teens / early, mid, or late teens","Plural noun: the period from thirteen to nineteen, or people of those ages.","Late teens identifies the later part of the thirteen-to-nineteen period.")],[M("She learned to drive in her teens, when she was in her seventies.","She learned to drive in her teens, when she was seventeen.","In one’s teens refers to ages thirteen through nineteen.","meaning")],[Q("teens.q1","teens.s1","meaning","If someone is in their mid-teens, about how old are they?","Around fifteen or sixteen.","Around five or six.","Around fifty or sixty.","The teens are the ages thirteen through nineteen."),Q("teens.q2","teens.s1","context","What does “in her late teens” mean?","She was near the end of the thirteen-to-nineteen age range.","She was in the final days of her life.","She was in her late twenties.","Late teens refers to the later teenage years."),Q("teens.q3","teens.s1","distinction","Which age is in the teens?","Nineteen.","Twelve.","Twenty.","Nineteen ends the thirteen-to-nineteen range."),Q("teens.q4","teens.s1","usage","Which phrase is standard?","He started college in his teens.","He started college in his teen.","He teens started college.","The age period is conventionally expressed as in one’s teens.")]);
P("teeth","Irregular plural of tooth, an inherited Germanic word with cognates such as German Zahn.",[C("teeth.s1","health","The dentist checked her teeth for cracks and cavities.","牙醫檢查她的牙齒是否有裂痕或蛀牙。","brush, clean, or check one’s teeth","Plural noun: the set of hard structures used to bite and chew.","Teeth is the plural form of tooth and names the structures used in biting and chewing.")],[M("The child used her teeth to hear the music more clearly.","The child used her teeth to bite and chew the apple.","Teeth are hard structures used to bite and chew, not to hear.","meaning")],[Q("teeth.q1","teeth.s1","meaning","What are teeth used for?","Biting and chewing food.","Sending messages over a wire.","Measuring temperature from a remote point.","Teeth are the hard structures used to bite and chew."),Q("teeth.q2","teeth.s1","grammar","What is the singular form of teeth?","tooth","teeths","teethes","Teeth is the irregular plural of tooth."),Q("teeth.q3","teeth.s1","context","Why did the dentist examine the child’s teeth?","To check the structures used for biting and chewing.","To see whether the child could transmit a telegram.","To measure the child’s height remotely.","The context is a dental check of the teeth."),Q("teeth.q4","teeth.s1","word-choice","Which sentence is correct?","The puppy is cutting its first teeth.","The puppy is cutting its first tooths.","The puppy is teething its first toothes.","Teeth is the correct irregular plural form.")]);
P("tele","A casual shortening of television, especially in British English; it is not the Greek combining form tele- “far” in this use.",[C("tele.s1","conversation","We watched the final on tele after dinner.","晚餐後我們在電視上看了決賽。","on tele","Noun: television, in casual speech, especially British English.","The informal expression stands for television as a medium or set.")],[M("They watched the match on tele, listening to it only through a telephone receiver.","They watched the match on tele, seeing the broadcast on television.","In casual speech tele means television, not a telephone call.","meaning")],[Q("tele.q1","tele.s1","meaning","In casual British speech, what does “on tele” mean?","On television.","By telegraph machine.","By remote measurement only.","Tele is a casual shortening of television in this use."),Q("tele.q2","tele.s1","context","If a match is on tele tonight, where can viewers watch it?","On a television broadcast.","Only in a telegram delivered by hand.","Inside a measuring telescope.","The phrase refers to television."),Q("tele.q3","tele.s1","distinction","Does tele in “watch it on tele” mean the Greek prefix for far?","No; it is a casual shortening of television.","Yes; it means the viewer is far away.","No; it means a person aged thirteen to nineteen.","This standalone noun is clipped from television, unlike the combining form tele-."),Q("tele.q4","tele.s1","register","Which use matches the informal noun tele?","We heard the result on tele.","The tele of the satellite sent measurements.","She tele the data yesterday.","The informal noun appears in phrases such as on tele.")]);
P("telecom","A clipping of telecommunication or telecommunications, from tele- “far” + communication.",[C("telecom.s1","industry","The telecom provider expanded fibre service to the rural district.","電信業者將光纖服務擴展到偏遠地區。","telecom + provider, industry, or network","Noun: the business or technology of sending information over a distance by cable, radio, or fibre.","The provider belongs to the telecommunications business and technology.")],[M("The telecom company delivered letters by horse and had no way to send information at a distance.","The telecom company carried voice and data over long-distance networks.","Telecom concerns technology or business for sending information over a distance.","meaning")],[Q("telecom.q1","telecom.s1","meaning","What field does telecom refer to?","Technology and business for sending information over distance.","The study of teeth and chewing.","The age period from thirteen through nineteen.","Telecom is the business or technology of long-distance communication."),Q("telecom.q2","telecom.s1","context","Why might a rural telecom provider lay fibre cable?","To carry data to customers over distance.","To help customers chew food.","To measure rainfall without sending readings.","Telecom networks transmit information over distance."),Q("telecom.q3","telecom.s1","distinction","How does telecom differ from a telegram?","Telecom is an industry or technology; a telegram is a message sent by telegraph.","Telecom is one message; telegram is a whole industry.","Both words mean a telescope.","The source sense defines telecom broadly as business or technology."),Q("telecom.q4","telecom.s1","collocation","Which phrase is natural?","the telecom industry","the telecom of one apple","telecom down heavily as rain","Telecom commonly modifies industry or provider.")]);
